Subject: Re: Fwd: SIG: Request for full third-party/subprocessor roster (cloud, telemetry, support)

Priyom — started populating the sheet. Draft entries (short):
- AWS (prod eu-west-1, us-west-2) — compute, S3 backups, RDS. Access: Platform infra team; backups encrypted with AWS KMS (CMKs managed by Redwood) — contractual flow-down: standard subprocessor clause;
- GCP (staging) — test workloads only;
- Azure (CI runners for certain customers) — limited usage;
- HashiCorp Vault (HCP) — secrets management; integrates with KMS; HSM via AWS CloudHSM for keywraps;
- Datadog — telemetry/metrics/alerts (no raw customer PII; request traces anonymized);
- Sentry — error aggregation (scrubbing enabled; PII not stored by default);
- Intercom — customer support chat (customer email, timestamps; no raw prompts stored for enterprise customers per config);
- Zendesk — ticketing for hosted support (attachments handled per customer tocks)
- Postgres managed DB provider (AWS RDS).

I added country/region cells and a "data_access_notes" column in the sheet. Flagged HashiCorp and CloudHSM as "security critical". Attaching the roster draft as redwood_subprocessor_roster.xlsx (sheet: draft_v1).

